<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en" dir="ltr"><head><meta charSet="utf-8" data-next-head=""/><meta charSet="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" data-next-head=""/><meta http-equiv="X-UA-Compatible" content="IE=edge" data-next-head=""/><meta name="HandheldFriendly" content="True" data-next-head=""/><meta name="MobileOptimized" content="320" data-next-head=""/><link rel="canonical" href="https://www.va.gov/family-and-caregiver-benefits/survivor-compensation/dependency-indemnity-compensation/survivor-rates/" data-next-head=""/><meta property="og:url" content="https://www.va.gov/family-and-caregiver-benefits/survivor-compensation/dependency-indemnity-compensation/survivor-rates/" data-next-head=""/><meta property="og:type" content="website" data-next-head=""/><meta name="DC.Date" content="2026-09-22" data-next-head=""/><title data-next-head="">Current D.I.C. Rates For Spouses And Dependents | Veterans Affairs</title><meta name="description" content="Review 2026 VA Dependency and Indemnity Compensation (D.I.C.) rates for the surviving spouses and dependent children of Veterans. These VA survivor benefits are tax exempt. This means you won’t have to pay any taxes on your compensation payments. These rates are effective December 1, 2025." data-next-head=""/><link rel="image_src" href="https://www.va.gov/img/design/logo/va-og-image.png" data-next-head=""/><meta property="og:site_name" content="Veterans Affairs" data-next-head=""/><meta property="og:title" content="Current D.I.C. rates for spouses and dependents | Veterans Affairs" data-next-head=""/><meta property="og:description" content="Review 2026 VA Dependency and Indemnity Compensation (D.I.C.) rates for the surviving spouses and dependent children of Veterans. These VA survivor benefits are tax exempt. This means you won’t have to pay any taxes on your compensation payments. These rates are effective December 1, 2025." data-next-head=""/><meta property="og:image" content="https://www.va.gov/img/design/logo/va-og-image.png" data-next-head=""/><meta property="og:image:alt" content="U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs" data-next-head=""/><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" data-next-head=""/><meta name="twitter:description" content="Review 2026 VA D.I.C. (Dependency and Indemnity Compensation) rates for the surviving spouses and dependent children of Veterans. These VA survivor benefits are tax exempt. This means you won’t have to pay any taxes on your D.I.C. payments." data-next-head=""/><meta name="twitter:site" content="@DeptVetAffairs" data-next-head=""/><meta name="twitter:title" content="Current D.I.C. rates for spouses and dependents | Veterans Affairs" data-next-head=""/><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://www.va.gov/img/design/logo/va-og-image.png" data-next-head=""/><meta name="twitter:image:alt" content="U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preconnect" href="https://www.googletagmanager.com"/><link href="/img/design/icons/apple-touch-icon.png" rel="apple-touch-icon-precomposed"/><link href="/img/design/icons/apple-touch-icon-72x72.png" rel="apple-touch-icon-precomposed" sizes="72x72"/><link href="/img/design/icons/apple-touch-icon-114x114.png" rel="apple-touch-icon-precomposed" sizes="114x114"/><link href="/img/design/icons/apple-touch-icon-152x152.png" rel="apple-touch-icon-precomposed" sizes="144x144"/><link rel="shortcut icon" sizes="any" href="/img/design/icons/favicon.ico"/><link nonce="1sjTItZVxy9ajFhOuwgx3kIFvUPWOTKb" rel="preload" href="/_next/static/chunks/1u1qi4l-ezvo3.css" as="style"/><link nonce="1sjTItZVxy9ajFhOuwgx3kIFvUPWOTKb" rel="preload" href="/_next/static/chunks/00x-ogb7yajny.css" as="style"/><link href="https://prod-va-gov-assets.s3-us-gov-west-1.amazonaws.com/generated/static-pages.css" data-entry-name="static-pages.css" rel="stylesheet"/><link rel="stylesheet" href="https://prod-va-gov-assets.s3-us-gov-west-1.amazonaws.com/generated/style.css"/><link rel